---
// "Show, don't assert." Three rendered surfaces, one per honesty principle:
//  a cited number · a number that carries its own confidence · the coach refusing.
// Every claim shown is structural (what the product does), not a novel research finding.
---

<section id="honesty" class="scroll-mt-20 border-t border-line bg-sunk/40 py-20 md:py-28">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="eyebrow rise">The honesty contract, rendered</p>
      <h2 class="rise mt-4 text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.9rem)]">
        The most persuasive thing we can show you is the product holding back.
      </h2>
      <p class="rise mt-6 text-lg text-ink-soft">
        These are the three moves that define it: name the method, carry the confidence, and refuse
        what it has no business answering. Here is each one, exactly as it appears.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <!-- 1 · a cited number -->
      <figure class="surface rise flex flex-col p-6" aria-label="Example: an estimate that names its method">
        <figcaption class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
          <span class="eyebrow">VO&#8322;max &middot; estimate</span>
          <span class="chip chip-accent chip-dot">Established</span>
        </figcaption>
        <hr class="hairline my-5" />
        <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
          <span class="mono text-4xl tracking-tight">42.1</span>
          <span class="mono text-sm text-ink-faint">ml/kg/min</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Estimated from resting inputs with the Jurca (2005) non-exercise model &mdash; not a
          treadmill test, and labelled as an estimate wherever it appears.
        </p>
        <dl class="mono mt-5 grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-x-4 gap-y-1.5 text-xs text-ink-faint">
          <dt>method</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Jurca 2005, non-exercise</dd>
          <dt>inputs</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">6 of 6 present</dd>
          <dt>note</dt><dd class="text-accent-soft">read the evidence &#8250;</dd>
        </dl>
      </figure>

      <!-- 2 · a number carrying its confidence -->
      <figure class="surface rise flex flex-col p-6" aria-label="Example: a number that carries coverage, freshness, origin and grade">
        <figcaption class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
          <span class="eyebrow">Overnight HRV &middot; RMSSD</span>
          <span class="chip chip-dot">confidence: fair</span>
        </figcaption>
        <hr class="hairline my-5" />
        <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
          <span class="mono text-4xl tracking-tight">48</span>
          <span class="mono text-sm text-ink-faint">ms</span>
          <span class="mono ml-auto self-end text-xs text-ink-faint">vs your normal 44&plusmn;7</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Every number ships with the four things that decide whether to trust it &mdash; so you
          always know how much weight it can bear.
        </p>
        <dl class="mono mt-5 grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-x-4 gap-y-1.5 text-xs text-ink-faint">
          <dt>coverage</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">6.1 h of 7.4 h slept</dd>
          <dt>freshness</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">last night</dd>
          <dt>origin</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">on-device sensor</dd>
          <dt>grade</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Established</dd>
        </dl>
      </figure>

      <!-- 3 · the coach refusing -->
      <figure class="surface rise flex flex-col p-6" aria-label="Example: the coach refusing a medical question">
        <figcaption class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
          <span class="eyebrow">Coach</span>
          <span class="chip chip-warn chip-dot">refused by design</span>
        </figcaption>
        <hr class="hairline my-5" />
        <p class="mono text-xs text-ink-faint">you asked</p>
        <p class="mt-1.5 font-serif text-lg leading-snug">&ldquo;Do I have sleep apnea?&rdquo;</p>
        <p class="mono mt-5 text-xs text-ink-faint">coach</p>
        <p class="mt-1.5 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          I can&rsquo;t diagnose that, and I won&rsquo;t try. Your overnight SpO&#8322; and
          breathing-rate trends are on your Sleep page for you and a clinician to read &mdash; but
          apnea is a medical diagnosis that needs a sleep study. Please raise it with a doctor.
        </p>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <p class="rise mono mt-8 text-xs text-ink-faint">
      Medical, diagnostic, and emergency questions are refused deterministically &mdash; a hard
      guardrail the language model cannot override, even with a perfect citation.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
